numerate"],"finding":"The new _GROUP_RECOVERABILITY ranking (Change 2) is named as an ordering over the ResolutionClass vocabulary, but the plan only specifies two coarse buckets (any-retryable leg wins; all-non-retryable → CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL) and never defines the ordering WITHIN the retryable pair (WAIT_AND_RETRY vs RETRY_NOW). A group whose legs classify to different retryable classes has no pinned winner, and the acceptance oracle only exercises a single 429→WAIT_AND_RETRY leg, so it does not disambiguate the table.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9cf6503363117b46","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan → Change 2 (`_GROUP_RECOVERABILITY`, `_classify_fallback_group`); Acceptance Criteria line 2 ('classifies as the retryable class, order-independent')","norm_id":"n7d1a4f2e8d4c95b0","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A FallbackExceptionGroup whose primary leg is a connection blip (RETRY_NOW) and whose fallback leg is a rate-limit 429 (WAIT_AND_RETRY) — which class the group reports is undefined, so the operator's stderr message (RESOLUTION_MESSAGES) is nondeterministic across implementations."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State the ordering explicitly, e.g. RETRY_NOW > WAIT_AND_RETRY > (all non-retryable) → CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL, and add an AC row for a group of [RETRY_NOW leg, WAIT_AND_RETRY leg] asserting the chosen winner.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the pydantic-ai 1.107.2 `FallbackModel.request` internal behavior (bare `raise exc` on a false-predicate leg discarding the collected primary group; group built only on `continue`-exhaustion) with a citable artifact — a source excerpt from the pinned wheel or a minimal reproduction test — rather than an unbacked 'Confirmed against installed pydantic-ai 1.107.2' assertion.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'In 1.107.2 the loop does `raise exc` for a leg whose predicate is False — bare-reraising that terminal leg and DISCARDING the collected primary 429 (the FallbackExceptionGroup is only built when the loop EXHAUSTS via continue).'","resolve_symbol: pydantic_ai.models.fallback.FallbackModel EXISTS (site-packages) — confirms the class, not the request() loop's raise-vs-continue branch.","ABSENCE: my repo-scoped tools cannot read .venv/site-packages/pydantic_ai/models/fallback.py to verify the raise/continue control flow; the plan pins no test or transcript demonstrating that Change 1 (never bare-reraise a fallback leg) is necessary because of THIS loop shape rather than an alternative."],"finding":"The pivotal root-cause premise — pydantic-ai 1.107.2 FallbackModel.request does a bare `raise exc` for a fallback leg whose fallback_on predicate is False, DISCARDING the collected primary 429, and builds the FallbackExceptionGroup only when the loop exhausts via `continue` — is an internal-behavior claim about installed third-party code that repo-scoped Grep/Read cannot reach (the file is under .venv/site-packages). resolve_symbol confirms FallbackModel exists but not the loop semantics. The plan asserts 'Confirmed against installed pydantic-ai 1.107.2' but cites no reproduction artifact (test/log) grounding that specific internal control flow.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f762792a7ebd2ce51","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Report §'Proven root cause (H1 wins)' bullets 3–4; caused_by/attribution","norm_id":"nabf6b93baf6a7063","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If 1.107.2 in fact already retains the primary group (e.g. the loop appends every leg and raises the group), Change 1's marker plumbing is unnecessary and the e2e 'revert Change 1 → INDETERMINATE' mutation would not reproduce, invalidating that acceptance gate.","A pin bump could change this internal behavior, silently defeating the marker approach."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add the exact `FallbackModel.request` source lines (or a tiny standalone reproduction that raises a keyless-fallback TypeError through a real FallbackModel and asserts the primary 429 is discarded) to the root-cause comments, so the raise-vs-continue premise the whole fix depends on is verifiable and pin-anchored.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State (and verify in the oracle) the precondition that Change 1 relies on wrap_candidate having actually wrapped the candidate, and specify the behavior when the wrapper is absent (documented acceptable degrade vs. a fallback stamping path that does not depend on the tracing wrapper).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tracing.py 195-202: wrap_candidate returns `model` unchanged if `_candidate_wrapper_class()` raises (pydantic-ai absent) or `cls(...)` raises.","Plan: 'build_fallback_model already wraps EVERY candidate in tracing._TracedCandidateModel' and 'best-effort; slotted exceptions degrade to the narrow predicate' — the acknowledged degrade path is only the per-exception stamp failure, not the wrapper-never-built case."],"finding":"The plan states wrap_candidate 'already wraps EVERY candidate' and Change 1's marker 'rides the existing per-candidate wrapper', but wrap_candidate returns the ORIGINAL unwrapped model when the WrapperModel class cannot be built or its construction raises (tracing.py 195-202). The plan's degrade story covers only the slotted-exception case ('slotted exceptions degrade to the narrow predicate'); it does not address the wrapper-absent case, in which no candidate is wrapped, no leg is ever stamped, and Change 1 silently no-ops fleet-wide.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc15523c4154b94df","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan §'Change 1', tracing.py wrap_candidate","norm_id":"nb45d31ae3d65b4a6","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the WrapperModel import/construction fails (or is monkey-degraded), every candidate is the bare provider model, the fallback leg is never stamped, is_fallback_leg_failure returns False, and the fallback TypeError again masks the primary 429 → INDETERMINATE — the exact bug, un-fixed, with no signal."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Note explicitly that when wrap_candidate degrades to the unwrapped model the marker cannot ride it, and either accept that degrade in writing (tracing already best-effort, and an absent WrapperModel implies pydantic-ai issues that would fail earlier) or move the leg-marker onto a seam independent of the optional tracing wrapper.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a guard that ties the fix to the assumed pydantic-ai loop behavior (e.g. an e2e assertion that a forced-True terminal leg yields a FallbackExceptionGroup, or a documented version-pin assertion) so a pydantic-ai upgrade that changes the request-loop semantics fails loudly rather than silently re-introducing INDETERMINATE.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decisi